<ContentLayout title="Editorial Policy – How We Write Our Car Guides" h1="Editorial policy" path="/editorial-policy" updated="2026-10-06" description="How the BamaMotors editorial team researches, writes, fact-checks and updates its Alabama car buying guides, and how we keep advertising separate.">
  <div class="prose">
    <p class="snippet">BamaMotors guides are written for Alabama car shoppers by the BamaMotors Editorial Team. We research official sources, explain things in plain English, show when each guide was last updated, and never let dealers or advertisers pay for editorial coverage.</p>
    <h2>How we research</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We rely on primary sources: the Alabama Department of Revenue, the Federal Trade Commission, the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau, NHTSA and the National Motor Vehicle Title Information System.</li>
      <li>We link to those sources inside each guide so you can verify every claim.</li>
      <li>We avoid inventing statistics. Price ranges on our city pages are calculated live from real listings on BamaMotors.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>How we keep guides current</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Evergreen guides are reviewed every 6–12 months; financing and price guides every 1–3 months.</li>
      <li>The "Updated" date only changes when a guide is substantially revised.</li>
      <li>Found something out of date? <a href="/contact">Tell us</a> and we will review it.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Independence</h2>
    <p>Dealers can pay for subscriptions and featured listings, and the site may display ads. None of this affects what we write. Featured listings are clearly labeled "Featured", and ads are kept separate from editorial content.</p>
    <h2>Reviews</h2>
    <p>Dealer reviews come only from signed-in shoppers and are moderated before they appear. We do not publish paid, incentivized or fabricated reviews.</p>
    <p><a href="/authors/bamamotors-editorial-team">Meet the BamaMotors Editorial Team →</a></p>
  </div>
</ContentLayout>
